# F5 routing/domain-bucket eval corpus (SEED). Ground truth for `scripts/eval_routing.py`.
# `route` is required + always scored. `domain_bucket` is scored ONLY for coding tickets with a
# NON-EMPTY, VERIFIED bucket — leave it "" when unverified (route-only scoring) rather than guess:
# a wrong ground-truth label poisons the eval worse than an unscored one.
#
# STATUS OF THESE ROWS (checked against live Jira, 2026-08-07). An earlier version of this header
# said "Each row = one closed MM ticket". That was false: only MM-14065 and MM-13527 are closed, and
# they are exactly the two `rca` rows — every `coding` row below is Open or In-Dev. The claim
# mattered because the harness leaned on it to argue the replay was blind.
#
# LEAKAGE, and why the harness now scrubs its input. 7 of the 7 `coding` rows have OPEN PRs whose
# titles name both the target repo and the domain; 0 of the 2 `rca` rows have any. "Does a PR exist
# for this ticket?" is therefore a near-perfect route oracle over this corpus — and research.md
# MANDATES the `gh pr list --search "<TICKET>"` that would find them. Several of those PRs were
# authored by this pipeline itself. eval_routing.py now replays from title+description only, with the
# worker's tools reduced to Write, so none of that is reachable. Keep it that way: adding a row does
# NOT require the ticket to be closed, but the harness must never be given a live ticket id to look up.
#
# EXPAND THIS to ~30 tickets with human-verified labels before trusting the accuracy number (the
